            "why": "A reader asks what you called and what you passed it. Both names sat in the `variable` family and read as one colour in 40 of 65 themes — in gruvbox-dark-medium both at #83a598 — so a call spent three to five colours inside and none of them on the two words that answer. Canon splits by language SURFACE rather than by call against definition: html, Vue, JSX, Liquid, Handlebars and MediaWiki's own `{{T|name=v}}` all take entity.other.attribute-name for a named argument on a tag or template surface. Under the argument's own family the pair read 25 of 65; under the surface's, 57.",
